|Description = less photographers photographing an Illinois Bell Telephone employee who is installing public telephone booths on Astor Street in Chicago ahead of the 1952 presidential conventions in that city<br>original caption published with photo: Swift installation of public telephones was good "news" to members of the press, radio, and television keeping a 24 hour vigil at Astor Street. Telephone men had booths in operation an hour after they arrived.
|Source = https://archive.org/details/belltelephonevol3132mag00amerrich/page/n148/mode/1up Bell Telephone Magazine Volume XXXI, 1952 (Spring 1952) page 133
